# snap-packaged CUPS on the desktop: its refresh wrapper runs the daemon start/
# stop scripts with `set -x`, dumping the whole shell trace plus exec/lifecycle
# chatter. All benign desktop-printing noise; a genuine crash still surfaces via
# systemd (snap.cups.*.service: Main process exited / dumped), which stays visible.
^\w{3} [ :[:digit:]]{11} [._[:alnum:]-]+ cups\.(cupsd|cups-browsed)\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (\+( |$)|==> |exec( |$)|echo( |$)|cat( |$)|true$|Terminated$| )
^[[:digit:]]{4}-[[:digit:]]{2}-[[:digit:]]{2}T[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2}\.[[:digit:]]+[+-][[:digit:]]{2}:[[:digit:]]{2} [._[:alnum:]-]+ cups\.(cupsd|cups-browsed)\[[[:digit:]]+\]: (\+( |$)|==> |exec( |$)|echo( |$)|cat( |$)|true$|Terminated$| )
